  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "039f6a39d2c22c8ad20a186febae0c8444d060a6bb0d39fa370dd32fd06ac884",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-039f6a39d2c2-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that any injury cognizable under \u00a7\u202f1964(c) is necessarily suffered at the plaintiff\u2019s residence, adopting a bright\u2011line rule similar to the Seventh Circuit\u2019s approach."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "039f6a39d2c22c8ad20a186febae0c8444d060a6bb0d39fa370dd32fd06ac884",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-039f6a39d2c2-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 16,
              "start": 16
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners further rely on the principle of\u202fmobilia sequuntur personam, which they say generally locates intangible property at the domicile of its owner, thereby locating Smagin\u2019s alleged injury at his residence."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Vincent Levy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3637675ef23b-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Vincent Levy, vincent Levy cites RJR\u202fNabisco, noting that the Court held private plaintiffs may sue under civil RICO for treble damages if they suffer a domestic injury."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Levy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Levy, levy also argues that the Court should look to the Restatement rules to determine where the injury was found and where it occurred."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Nicholas O. Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Nicholas O. Kennedy points out that Mr. Smagin\u2019s RICO claim is based on alleged injury to his California property, and that a domestic injury is one that arises in the United States."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "039f6a39d2c22c8ad20a186febae0c8444d060a6bb0d39fa370dd32fd06ac884",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-039f6a39d2c2-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court, applying its extraterritoriality framework, held that \u00a7\u202f1964(c) does not overcome the presumption that RICO\u2019s private cause of action applies only to domestic injuries because Congress gave no clear indication it intended to create such a right for injuries abroad."
      }
    ],
